Other bundled material
----------------------
- Colour palettes (eleven, in three groups; docs/palettes.md in the source repository): the historical colour palettes follow the
  colour conventions of Axman and Depthmap (Dalton, N. (1988), Axman [software], University College London; Turner, A. (2001),
  Depthmap: a program to perform visibility graph analysis, Proceedings of the 3rd International Symposium on Space Syntax,
  Atlanta, 31.1-31.9). The Axmanesque palette takes its name from Axman. rPSTool implements the palettes in R using hexadecimal colour values
  and independently written colour mapping functions; no depthmapX source code is included. Two white-background adaptations
  (Axmanesque White, depthmapX Classic White) reuse some of the historical colours; two palettes (Coral Night, Coral Day) were
  designed for rPSTool. The Blue-Red and Purple-Orange values coincide, in reversed order, with the 7-class ColorBrewer RdYlBu and
  PuOr schemes and are attributed to Cynthia Brewer (http://colorbrewer.org/).
- Example data (inst/extdata/hillier_iida/): the Barnsbury example is derived from Hillier, B. and Iida, S. (2005), Network and
  Psychological Effects in Urban Movement, LNCS 3693, pp. 475-490 (DOI 10.1007/11556114_30); the original data were obtained from
  https://discovery.ucl.ac.uk/id/eprint/1232/. The movement gate-count observations are redistributed with the authors' permission.
  The axial network and unlinks are adapted from the source material, with geometries georeferenced to EPSG:27700 and spatially
  transformed (best-fit transformation) by Kimon Krenz; the coordinates are therefore not the original coordinates. The original
  research and data remain attributable to their respective authors. The movement gate counts were originally reported by Penn, A.,
  Hillier, B., Banister, D. and Xu, J. (1998), Configurational modelling of urban movement networks, Environment and Planning B:
  Planning and Design, 25(1), pp. 59-84 (DOI 10.1068/b250059). The package licence (LGPL-3-or-later) applies to rPSTool's software
  and does not relicense the example data (docs/example-data.md).
